***********************************************************************
*                    EMC - INSTALLATION GUIDE                         *
***********************************************************************

1. EXTRACT THE ARCHIVE
   Open your terminal and run these commands to extract the files:

   cd ~/Downloads
   tar -xvf EMC_INSTALL_standalone.tar.gz -C ~

2. RUN INSTALLATION
   Start the base installer script:

   ~/EMC_install/EMC_standalone_base_installer.sh 

   The installer guides you through four stages:
   - Step 1 (Preinstall)    : Prepare the installation media (ISO/USB).
   - Step 2 (Install Debian): Install Debian minimal System.
   - Step 3 (Install EMC)   : System deployment and package installation.
   - Step 4 (Postinstall)   : Final setup and reboot.

   Use the 'help' command within each menu for further guidance!

See Documentation on github: https://github.com/xdpetx/EMC-Commander-beta

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
-                      AFTER INSTALLATION ...                         -
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

EMC Commander start instructions:

   1. After reboot, boot the partition where EMC Commander is installed.
   2. After login, start EMC Commander with: startx
   3. When EMC has started you will see a Mainbar info notify for first instructions.
   4. To install software open EMC Configuration Toolbar how described in Mainbar info.

The launchers are pre-configured. If an application is missing, you 
will receive a notification at startup. You can install missing apps 
via the 'App Installer' (accessible via the mainbar info window).

Use EMC Configuration Toolbar to edit configuration files.
- Scroll UP/DOWN on an icon in launchbar to see its tooltip.
- dbl-click space in the mainbar to open EMC Configuration Toolbar.

CONFIGURATION FILES:
- Launchbars, Tooltips & Icons: $HOME/.config/polybar/usr/
- Workspace Icons             : $HOME/.config/i3/usr/config_workspaces
- Autostart/Commands          : $HOME/.config/i3/usr/config_usercommands

MONITOR CONFIG
-actual resolution            : $HOME/.config/polybar/usr/monitor.ini
-resolution templates         : $HOME/.config/polybar/usr/monitor

LOG FILES:
- Installer logs and system reports are stored in: $HOME/.config/polybar/log

See Documentation on github: https://github.com/xdpetx/EMC-Commander-beta/blob/main/README_config.md

